{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And if you bring a meal-offering of first-fruits</b> — now, if [the word] אִם functions with the force of כִּי ['when/for'], for this is not optional, since the verse is speaking of the meal-offering of the omer, which is an obligation, and likewise 'And if the Jubilee belongs to the children of Israel' (Numbers 36:4) — this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Leviticus 2:14). But the correct interpretation is that because He is not now commanding them to perform this commandment, He spoke thus. He says: when you bring a griddle meal-offering, you shall make it thus, and if you bring a pan meal-offering, thus shall you make it, and if it is a meal-offering of first-fruits, the meal-offering that you bring — according to this rule you shall make it. And behold, the 'if' is according to its plain sense. And the reason for 'And if the Jubilee belongs to the children of Israel' (Numbers 36:4) is that they said: even if the children of Israel inherit the land for all time and merit to sanctify the Jubilee year, the inheritance will not revert to us. And it is also possible that He said, 'And if you bring a meal-offering of first-fruits, thus shall you make it,' as if to say: if YHWH your Elohim brings you into the land and you reap its harvest and you bring a meal-offering of first-fruits, thus shall you make it — for the inheritance of the land He mentions to them conditionally, as He said (Deuteronomy 11:22–23), 'If you shall surely keep all this commandment, etc., and YHWH will dispossess all these nations from before you,' and similarly in many places."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:49:53.976522192Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}